# ---- MCMC output --------------------------------------------------------
# Fitted posterior samples are large (tens of MB) and fully regenerable by
# re-running the scripts. Keeping them out of history avoids permanent repo
# bloat. Figures and summary tables under output/ ARE tracked, since they are
# small and serve as a record of each fit.
*.rds

# ---- Rendered reports ---------------------------------------------------
# The rendered HTML under reports/ IS tracked deliberately, so collaborators
# who don't run R can open the current results straight from the repo. It is
# self-contained (~2.4 MB) and is rewritten on every render, so each render
# adds a full copy to history -- re-render only when the results change, not
# as a matter of routine.

# ---- R session artefacts ------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
.Rproj.user/
*_cache/
*-Ex.R

# NIMBLE compiles model code to C++ in a temporary project directory
nimble_generatedCode*/

# ---- Editor / IDE (machine-specific) ------------------------------------
.posit/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local settings (per-machine permissions, not shared config)
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---- Office lock files --------------------------------------------------
# Word/Excel write a hidden ~$name.docx alongside any open document. They are
# transient, machine-specific, and appear and vanish as files are opened.
~$*

# ---- OS junk ------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
._*

# Manuscript materials ----------------------------------------------------
# Ignore the working directory (rendered HTML, Quarto's PLAN_files/ asset
# bundle, Word drafts) but KEEP manuscript/figures/ and PLAN.md -- the figures
# are generated deliverables, and PLAN.md carries the model specification and
# the record of decisions behind the analysis. PLAN.html is the render of
# PLAN.md and stays ignored, along with its PLAN_files/ asset bundle.
#
# Note the trailing /* rather than a plain `manuscript/`. Git will not descend
# into an excluded directory, so `manuscript/` followed by
# `!manuscript/figures/` silently fails: the negation can never be reached.
# Excluding the CONTENTS instead leaves the directory itself visible, which is
# what allows a subdirectory to be re-included.
#
# This rule also sat here for a while with no effect, because 14 files under
# manuscript/ were already tracked and Git will not ignore a tracked file.
# They were untracked with `git rm -r --cached manuscript` on 2026-08-14;
# earlier versions remain in history.
manuscript/*
!manuscript/figures/
!manuscript/PLAN.md

# ---- Misc ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.bak
*~
